(13. TRIES AND UNION-FIND) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A trie, or prefix tree, stores strings character by character. Each edge is labelled with a) Tj T*
(character, and each path from the root spells a prefix. Looking up a word of length L takes) Tj T*
(O\(L\) time, no matter how many words are stored. Tries are used for autocomplete and spell) Tj T*
(checking because all words with a given prefix sit in one subtree.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A union-find structure, also called a disjoint-set structure, keeps track of which elements) Tj T*
(belong to the same group. Find returns the representative of an element's group, and union) Tj T*
(merges two groups. With union by rank and path compression, a sequence of operations runs in) Tj T*
(nearly constant amortized time per operation. Kruskal's algorithm uses union-find to detect) Tj T*
(cycles.) Tj T*
ET
